--- b1 medium.en: Open enrollment ends on December 7, and one choice you make this fall can be very hard to undo. It is the choice between Medicare Advantage and a Medigap plan. Medicare itself warns that in most cases, if you drop a Medigap policy to join an Advantage plan, you may not be able to get it back. And in some cases, you may not be able to get any Medigap policy at all. Here is what the official rules say.
